          "finish_reason": "length",
          "answer_excerpt": "# Technical Analysis of Plant Condition Monitoring Records\n\n## 1. Scope and Data Overview\n\nThis report analyzes 18 condition-monitoring records (Records 0000000\u20130000017) drawn from a mixed fleet of rotating and static process equipment: reactors, heat exchangers, turbines, compressors, separators, condensers, a pipeline segment, a valve, and a scrubber. Each record contains five measured parameters:\n\n- **Pressure** (kPa)\n- **Temperature** (\u00b0C)\n- **Flow** (m\u00b3/h)\n- **Vibration** (mm/s RMS)\n- **Efficiency** (%)\n\nBecause the records span heterogeneous asset classes, the analysis below is structured in three parts: (1) fleet-wide screening against typical alarm thresholds, (2) asset-class-specific interpretation of the most concerning units, and (3) a prioritized maintenance action plan. Where absolute design baselines are unavailable, thresholds are drawn from common industry practice (e.g., ISO 10816/20816 vibration zones, typical thermal performance bands) and flagged as assumptions.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Fleet-Wide Screening\n\n### 2.1 Vibration \u2014 the dominant anomaly\n\nUsing ISO 10816-3 style zones for machines on rigid foundations",
