          "answer_excerpt": "# Technical Analysis of Plant Condition-Monitoring Records (Records 0000000\u20130000017)\n\n## 1. Scope and Method\n\nThis report analyzes 18 condition-monitoring records spanning six asset classes (reactors, heat exchangers, compressors, valves, turbines, pipelines, pumps, separators, condensers) across 17 stations. Each record contains five measured parameters: pressure (kPa), temperature (\u00b0C), flow (m\u00b3/h), vibration velocity (mm/s RMS), and efficiency (%).\n\nBecause the dataset lacks nameplate data, design operating points, and historical baselines, the analysis relies on:\n\n1. **Cross-asset benchmarking** \u2014 comparing each unit against the fleet distribution for its asset class.\n2. **Physical plausibility screening** \u2014 flagging measurements inconsistent with the expected thermodynamic or mechanical behavior of the equipment type.\n3. **ISO 10816/20816 vibration severity zones** \u2014 the standard framework for interpreting broadband vibration velocity on rotating machinery (Zone A: new/commissioned; Zone B: unrestricted long-term operation; Zone C: restricted operation/alarm; Zone D: danger/trip).\n\nFleet-wide summary statistics for context:\n\n| Parameter | Min | Max | Approx. Mean |\n|",
